  "goodToKnow": "Die Frömmigkeit is piety or devoutness. Fromm means pious: ein frommer Mensch, and also meek: fromm wie ein Lamm. Ein frommer Wunsch is wishful thinking. In the 17th and 18th centuries, Pietism, centred in Halle and Württemberg, stressed personal Frömmigkeit over doctrine. Die Scheinheiligkeit is false piety. It has no plural."
